IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc24-appeal-procedure.l4 -- the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Part XXI, sections 678 to 690:
-- Procedure on Appeals, Powers of the Court of Appeal, powers on appeal against sentence, the appellant's presence, restitution and forfeiture.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), part agent ccc24. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website
-- consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29 as ruled on 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-12). Every function answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN or a MAYBE of a type:
--   JUST TRUE   the text's words are met on the facts given.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words: a flat negative, a condition it introduces with "unless", "except", "only if", a period it fixes,
--               a "where"/"when"/"on" gate that fails (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05), or a duty's own "if" that fails.
--   NOTHING     not covered: a grant or power whose "if" or "with" gate fails (ruling of 2026-11-12), a scope limit with no "only", a list not closed, silent,
--               or pointing outside the text (rules of court, another part's section).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into JUST FALSE.
-- A function that answers a duty answers whether the duty applies on the facts; where the text fixes a number it answers compliance with it.
-- Tags in the comment blocks (`-- @tag grant=...`, `-- @tag fork=...`) are read by the generator of NOTES.md; they have no meaning in L4.

§ `Part XXI -- Appeals -- Indictable Offences -- Procedure on Appeals (sections 678 to 685)`

§§ `Section 678 -- Notice of appeal`

-- 678(1): notice "in such manner and within such period as may be directed by rules of court". The period is the rules' (outside the text): an input.
-- Fork F678: a notice outside the period answers NOTHING, because 678(2) lets the court extend the time "at any time"; the other reading is JUST FALSE.
-- @tag fork=F678
-- src:14140 | 678 (1) An appellant who proposes to appeal to the court of appeal or to obtain the leave of that court to appeal shall give notice of appeal or notice of his application for leave to appeal in such manner and within such period as may be directed by rules of court.
@ref s 678(1) (src:14140-14140)
GIVEN `the notice was given in the manner directed by rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days after which the notice was given` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days that rules of court allow for the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 678(1) the notice of appeal or of the application for leave to appeal was given in the manner and within the period directed by rules of court` MEANS
    IF `the notice was given in the manner directed by rules of court` AND `the number of days after which the notice was given` AT MOST `the number of days that rules of court allow for the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "in such manner and within such period as may be directed by rules of court"

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14142 | (2) The court of appeal or a judge thereof may at any time extend the time within which notice of appeal or notice of an application for leave to appeal may be given.
@ref s 678(2) (src:14142-14142)
GIVEN `the notice is notice of appeal or notice of an application for leave to appeal under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 678(2) the court of appeal or a judge may extend the time for giving notice of appeal or of an application for leave to appeal` MEANS
    IF `the notice is notice of appeal or notice of an application for leave to appeal under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may at any time extend the time within which notice of appeal or notice of an application for leave to appeal may be given"

-- 678.1: "Where a respondent cannot be found after reasonable efforts" is a where-gate on a grant: JUST FALSE by ruling (b), listed for a lawyer.
-- @tag grant=where
-- src:14144 | 678.1 Where a respondent cannot be found after reasonable efforts have been made to serve the respondent with a notice of appeal or notice of an application for leave to appeal, service of the notice of appeal or the notice of the application for leave to appeal may be effected substitutionally in the manner and within the period directed by a judge of the court of appeal.
@ref s 678.1 (src:14144-14144)
GIVEN `the respondent cannot be found after reasonable efforts have been made to serve the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 678.1 service of the notice of appeal or of the application for leave to appeal may be effected substitutionally` MEANS
    IF `the respondent cannot be found after reasonable efforts have been made to serve the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a respondent cannot be found after reasonable efforts have been made to serve the respondent"

§§ `Section 679 -- Release pending determination of appeal`

DECLARE `s 679(1) kind of appeal` IS ONE OF
    `s 679(1)(a) an appeal to the court of appeal against conviction`
    `s 679(1)(b) an appeal to the court of appeal against sentence only`
    `s 679(1)(c) an appeal or an application for leave to appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada`
    `s 679(1) an appeal of another kind`

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14146 | 679 (1) A judge of the court of appeal may, in accordance with this section, release an appellant from custody pending the determination of his appeal if,
-- src:14147 | (a) in the case of an appeal to the court of appeal against conviction, the appellant has given notice of appeal or, where leave is required, notice of his application for leave to appeal pursuant to section 678;
-- src:14148 | (b) in the case of an appeal to the court of appeal against sentence only, the appellant has been granted leave to appeal; or
-- src:14149 | (c) in the case of an appeal or an application for leave to appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada, the appellant has filed and served his notice of appeal or, where leave is required, his application for leave to appeal.
@ref s 679(1) (src:14146-14149)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 679(1) kind of appeal`
      `the appellant has given notice of appeal or, where leave is required, notice of the application for leave to appeal pursuant to section 678` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant has been granted leave to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant has filed and served the notice of appeal or, where leave is required, the application for leave to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 679(1) a judge of the court of appeal may release an appellant from custody pending the determination of the appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 679(1)(a) an appeal to the court of appeal against conviction` THEN
        IF `the appellant has given notice of appeal or, where leave is required, notice of the application for leave to appeal pursuant to section 678`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the appellant has given notice of appeal"
    WHEN `s 679(1)(b) an appeal to the court of appeal against sentence only` THEN
        IF `the appellant has been granted leave to appeal`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the appellant has been granted leave to appeal"
    WHEN `s 679(1)(c) an appeal or an application for leave to appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` THEN
        IF `the appellant has filed and served the notice of appeal or, where leave is required, the application for leave to appeal`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the appellant has filed and served his notice of appeal"
    WHEN `s 679(1) an appeal of another kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "(a) in the case of an appeal to the court of appeal against conviction"

-- src:14151 | (2) Where an appellant applies to a judge of the court of appeal to be released pending the determination of his appeal, he shall give written notice of the application to the prosecutor or to such other person as a judge of the court of appeal directs.
@ref s 679(2) (src:14151-14151)
GIVEN `the appellant applies to a judge of the court of appeal to be released pending the determination of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 679(2) the appellant must give written notice of the application for release to the prosecutor or to another person a judge of the court of appeal directs` MEANS
    IF `the appellant applies to a judge of the court of appeal to be released pending the determination of the appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an appellant applies to a judge of the court of appeal to be released"

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14153 | (3) In the case of an appeal referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (c), the judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of his appeal if the appellant establishes that
-- src:14154 | (a) the appeal or application for leave to appeal is not frivolous;
-- src:14155 | (b) he will surrender himself into custody in accordance with the terms of the order; and
-- src:14156 | (c) his detention is not necessary in the public interest.
@ref s 679(3) (src:14153-14156)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 679(1) kind of appeal`
      `the appellant establishes that the appeal or application for leave to appeal is not frivolous` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant establishes that he will surrender himself into custody in accordance with the terms of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant establishes that his detention is not necessary in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 679(3) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against conviction or to the Supreme Court of Canada` MEANS
    IF    (kind EQUALS `s 679(1)(a) an appeal to the court of appeal against conviction` OR kind EQUALS `s 679(1)(c) an appeal or an application for leave to appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada`)
      AND `the appellant establishes that the appeal or application for leave to appeal is not frivolous`
      AND `the appellant establishes that he will surrender himself into custody in accordance with the terms of the order`
      AND `the appellant establishes that his detention is not necessary in the public interest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the appellant establishes that"

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14158 | (4) In the case of an appeal referred to in paragraph (1)(b), the judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of his appeal or until otherwise ordered by a judge of the court of appeal if the appellant establishes that
-- src:14159 | (a) the appeal has sufficient merit that, in the circumstances, it would cause unnecessary hardship if he were detained in custody;
-- src:14160 | (b) he will surrender himself into custody in accordance with the terms of the order; and
-- src:14161 | (c) his detention is not necessary in the public interest.
@ref s 679(4) (src:14158-14161)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 679(1) kind of appeal`
      `the appellant establishes that the appeal has sufficient merit that, in the circumstances, it would cause unnecessary hardship if he were detained in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant establishes that he will surrender himself into custody in accordance with the terms of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant establishes that his detention is not necessary in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 679(4) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against sentence only` MEANS
    IF    kind EQUALS `s 679(1)(b) an appeal to the court of appeal against sentence only`
      AND `the appellant establishes that the appeal has sufficient merit that, in the circumstances, it would cause unnecessary hardship if he were detained in custody`
      AND `the appellant establishes that he will surrender himself into custody in accordance with the terms of the order`
      AND `the appellant establishes that his detention is not necessary in the public interest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the appellant establishes that"

-- src:14163 | (5) If the judge of the court of appeal does not refuse the appellant’s application, the judge shall make a release order referred to in section 515, the form of which may be adapted to suit the circumstances, which must include a condition that the accused surrender themselves into custody in accordance with the order.
@ref s 679(5) (src:14163-14163)
GIVEN `the judge of the court of appeal does not refuse the appellant's application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 679(5) the judge must make a release order referred to in section 515 that includes a condition that the accused surrender themselves into custody` MEANS
    IF `the judge of the court of appeal does not refuse the appellant's application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the judge of the court of appeal does not refuse the appellant's application"

-- @tag fork=F679i
-- src:14165 | (5.1) The person having the custody of the appellant shall, if the appellant complies with the release order, immediately release the appellant.
@ref s 679(5.1) (src:14165-14165)
GIVEN `the appellant complies with the release order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 679(5.1) the person having custody of the appellant must immediately release the appellant` MEANS
    IF `the appellant complies with the release order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the appellant complies with the release order"

-- The same duty as a regulative rule. "immediately" is modelled as WITHIN 0 (assumed, not ruled: the text gives no number); the unit of time is days.
DECLARE `s 679(5.1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 679(5.1) release the appellant`

-- @tag fork=F679i
@ref s 679(5.1) (src:14165-14165)
`s 679(5.1) the immediate release rule` MEANS
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison`
    MUST `s 679(5.1) release the appellant`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the keeper of a prison` BECAUSE "the appellant complied with the release order and was not immediately released"

-- 679(6): "Sections 495.1, 512.3 and 524 apply ... in respect of any proceedings under this section." A list that does not say "only": another section is not covered.
-- src:14167 | (6) Sections 495.1, 512.3 and 524 apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, in respect of any proceedings under this section.
@ref s 679(6) (src:14167-14167)
GIVEN `the section number` IS A NUMBER
      `the proceedings are proceedings under section 679` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 679(6) the section applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the proceedings under section 679` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings under section 679` AND (`the section number` EQUALS 495.1 OR `the section number` EQUALS 512.3 OR `the section number` EQUALS 524)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Sections 495.1, 512.3 and 524 apply"

-- src:14169 | (7) If, with respect to any person, the Minister of Justice gives a direction or makes a reference under section 696.3, this section applies to the release or detention of that person pending the hearing and determination of the reference as though that person were an appellant in an appeal described in paragraph (1)(a).
@ref s 679(7) (src:14169-14169)
GIVEN `the Minister of Justice has given a direction or made a reference under section 696.3 with respect to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 679(7) section 679 applies to the release or detention of the person pending the hearing and determination of the reference as though the person were an appellant in an appeal described in paragraph (1)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the Minister of Justice has given a direction or made a reference under section 696.3 with respect to the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, with respect to any person, the Minister of Justice gives a direction or makes a reference under section 696.3"

-- src:14171 | (7.1) Where, with respect to any person, the court of appeal or the Supreme Court of Canada orders a new trial, section 515 or 522, as the case may be, applies to the release or detention of that person pending the new trial or new hearing as though that person were charged with the offence for the first time, except that the powers of a justice under section 515 or of a judge under section 522 are exercised by a judge of the court of appeal.
@ref s 679(7.1) (src:14171-14171)
GIVEN `the court of appeal or the Supreme Court of Canada has ordered a new trial with respect to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 679(7.1) section 515 or 522 applies to the release or detention of the person pending the new trial or new hearing as though the person were charged with the offence for the first time, the powers being exercised by a judge of the court of appeal` MEANS
    IF `the court of appeal or the Supreme Court of Canada has ordered a new trial with respect to the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, with respect to any person, the court of appeal or the Supreme Court of Canada orders a new trial"

-- src:14173 | (8) This section applies to applications for leave to appeal and appeals to the Supreme Court of Canada in summary conviction proceedings.
@ref s 679(8) (src:14173-14173)
GIVEN `the application or appeal is an application for leave to appeal or an appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada in summary conviction proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 679(8) section 679 applies to the application for leave to appeal or the appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada in summary conviction proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the application or appeal is an application for leave to appeal or an appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada in summary conviction proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to applications for leave to appeal and appeals to the Supreme Court of Canada in summary conviction proceedings"

-- 679(10): directions for expediting. Two routes; both are "where"-gated (the first on the judge's own acts, the second on the SCC appellant's application).
-- @tag grant=where
-- src:14176 | (10) A judge of the court of appeal, where on the application of an appellant he does not make an order under subsection (5) or where he cancels an order previously made under this section, or a judge of the Supreme Court of Canada on application by an appellant in the case of an appeal to that Court, may give such directions as he thinks necessary for expediting the hearing of the appellant’s appeal or for expediting the new trial or new hearing or the hearing of the reference, as the case may be.
@ref s 679(10) (src:14176-14176)
GIVEN `the judge is a judge of the court of appeal and the appellant has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge does not make an order under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge cancels an order previously made under section 679` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is a judge of the Supreme Court of Canada and an appellant has applied in the case of an appeal to that Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 679(10) a judge may give the directions the judge thinks necessary for expediting the hearing of the appeal, the new trial, the new hearing or the hearing of the reference` MEANS
    IF    (    `the judge is a judge of the court of appeal and the appellant has applied`
           AND (`the judge does not make an order under subsection (5)` OR `the judge cancels an order previously made under section 679`))
       OR `the judge is a judge of the Supreme Court of Canada and an appellant has applied in the case of an appeal to that Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where on the application of an appellant he does not make an order under subsection (5) or where he cancels an order previously made"

-- The seam that ccc20 (ss 515, 522, 523) takes as an input (PLAN.md section 6): "the person has been released pending determination of an appeal".
-- JUST TRUE while the section 679 release is pending; JUST FALSE once the appeal is determined ("pending the determination": an until-bar, ruling (d) of 2026-11-05).
-- src:14146 | 679 (1) A judge of the court of appeal may, in accordance with this section, release an appellant from custody pending the determination of his appeal if,
@ref s 679(1) (src:14146-14146)
GIVEN `a judge of the court of appeal has made a release order under subsection 679(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal or the reference has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 679 the person has been released pending determination of an appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a judge of the court of appeal has made a release order under subsection 679(5)`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "release an appellant from custody pending the determination of his appeal"
        IF `the appeal or the reference has been determined`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "pending the determination of his appeal"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 680 -- Review by court of appeal`

DECLARE `s 680(1) kind of decision` IS ONE OF
    `s 680(1) a decision made by a judge under section 522`
    `s 680(1) a decision made under subsection 524(3) to (5), (6.1) or (6.2) with respect to an accused referred to in paragraph 524(1)(a)`
    `s 680(1) a decision made by a judge of the court of appeal under section 320.25 or 679`
    `s 680(1) a decision of another kind`

-- "on the direction of the chief justice": an "on"-gate on a grant, JUST FALSE by ruling (b), listed. "if it does not confirm the decision": an "if"-gate, NOTHING.
-- @tag grant=where
-- src:14178 | 680 (1) A decision made by a judge under section 522, a decision made under subsections 524(3) to (5), (6.1) or (6.2) with respect to an accused referred to in paragraph 524(1)(a) or a decision made by a judge of the court of appeal under section 320.25 or 679 may, on the direction of the chief justice or acting chief justice of the court of appeal, be reviewed by that court and that court may, if it does not confirm the decision,
-- src:14179 | (a) vary the decision; or
-- src:14180 | (b) substitute another decision that, in its opinion, should have been made.
@ref s 680(1) (src:14178-14180)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 680(1) kind of decision`
      `the chief justice or acting chief justice of the court of appeal has directed that the decision be reviewed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court of appeal does not confirm the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 680(1) the court of appeal may review the decision and vary it or substitute another decision that in its opinion should have been made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF kind EQUALS `s 680(1) a decision of another kind`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "A decision made by a judge under section 522"
        IF NOT `the chief justice or acting chief justice of the court of appeal has directed that the decision be reviewed`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the direction of the chief justice or acting chief justice of the court of appeal"
        IF `the court of appeal does not confirm the decision`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it does not confirm the decision"

-- @tag grant=where
-- src:14182 | (2) On consent of the parties, the powers of the court of appeal under subsection (1) may be exercised by a judge of that court.
@ref s 680(2) (src:14182-14182)
GIVEN `the parties consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 680(2) a judge of the court of appeal may exercise the powers of the court of appeal under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the parties consent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On consent of the parties"

-- src:14184 | (3) A decision as varied or substituted under this section shall have effect and may be enforced in all respects as though it were the decision originally made.
@ref s 680(3) (src:14184-14184)
