    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A decision as varied or substituted under this section"

§§ `Section 682 -- Report by judge, transcript, copies`

-- src:14187 | 682 (1) Where, under this Part, an appeal is taken or an application for leave to appeal is made, the judge or provincial court judge who presided at the trial shall, at the request of the court of appeal or a judge thereof, in accordance with rules of court, furnish it or him with a report on the case or on any matter relating to the case that is specified in the request.
@ref s 682(1) (src:14187-14187)
GIVEN `an appeal is taken or an application for leave to appeal is made under Part XXI` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court of appeal or a judge of it has requested a report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 682(1) the judge or provincial court judge who presided at the trial must furnish the court of appeal with a report on the case` MEANS
    IF `an appeal is taken or an application for leave to appeal is made under Part XXI` AND `the court of appeal or a judge of it has requested a report`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at the request of the court of appeal or a judge thereof"

DECLARE `s 682(2) material` IS ONE OF
    `s 682(2)(a) the evidence taken at the trial`
    `s 682(2)(b) any charge to the jury and any objections that were made to a charge to the jury`
    `s 682(2)(c) the reasons for judgment`
    `s 682(2)(d) the addresses of the prosecutor and the accused`
    `s 682(2) other material`

-- src:14189 | (2) A copy or transcript of
-- src:14190 | (a) the evidence taken at the trial,
-- src:14191 | (b) any charge to the jury and any objections that were made to a charge to the jury,
-- src:14192 | (c) the reasons for judgment, if any, and
-- src:14193 | (d) the addresses of the prosecutor and the accused, if a ground for the appeal is based on either of the addresses,
-- src:14194 | shall be furnished to the court of appeal, except in so far as it is dispensed with by order of a judge of that court.
@ref s 682(2) (src:14189-14194)
GIVEN material IS A `s 682(2) material`
      `the material exists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a ground for the appeal is based on either of the addresses` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy or transcript is dispensed with by order of a judge of the court of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 682(2) a copy or transcript of the material shall be furnished to the court of appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF material EQUALS `s 682(2) other material`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "A copy or transcript of"
        IF `the copy or transcript is dispensed with by order of a judge of the court of appeal`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in so far as it is dispensed with by order of a judge of that court"
        IF material EQUALS `s 682(2)(c) the reasons for judgment` AND (NOT `the material exists`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the reasons for judgment, if any"
        IF material EQUALS `s 682(2)(d) the addresses of the prosecutor and the accused` AND (NOT `a ground for the appeal is based on either of the addresses`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a ground for the appeal is based on either of the addresses"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

