§§ `Section 683 -- Powers of court of appeal`

DECLARE `s 683(1) power` IS ONE OF
    `s 683(1)(a) order the production of any writing, exhibit or other thing connected with the proceedings`
    `s 683(1)(b) order any witness who would have been a compellable witness at the trial to attend and be examined`
    `s 683(1)(c) admit, as evidence, an examination that is taken under subparagraph (b)(ii)`
    `s 683(1)(d) receive the evidence, if tendered, of any witness, including the appellant, who is a competent but not compellable witness`
    `s 683(1)(e) order that a question be referred for inquiry and report to a special commissioner`
    `s 683(1)(f) act on the report of a commissioner who is appointed under paragraph (e)`
    `s 683(1)(g) amend the indictment`

-- The common gate is "where it considers it in the interests of justice" (a where-gate: JUST FALSE, listed). Each paragraph's own descriptive condition is a limit on the grant: NOTHING.
-- Paragraph (g) is closed by "unless it is of the opinion that the accused has been misled or prejudiced": JUST FALSE.
-- @tag grant=where
-- @tag grant=closed
-- src:14201 | 683 (1) For the purposes of an appeal under this Part, the court of appeal may, where it considers it in the interests of justice,
-- src:14202 | (a) order the production of any writing, exhibit or other thing connected with the proceedings;
-- src:14203 | (b) order any witness who would have been a compellable witness at the trial, whether or not he was called at the trial,
-- src:14204 | (i) to attend and be examined before the court of appeal, or
-- src:14205 | (ii) to be examined in the manner provided by rules of court before a judge of the court of appeal, or before any officer of the court of appeal or justice of the peace or other person appointed by the court of appeal for the purpose;
-- src:14206 | (c) admit, as evidence, an examination that is taken under subparagraph (b)(ii);
-- src:14207 | (d) receive the evidence, if tendered, of any witness, including the appellant, who is a competent but not compellable witness;
-- src:14208 | (e) order that any question arising on the appeal that
-- src:14209 | (i) involves prolonged examination of writings or accounts, or scientific or local investigation, and
-- src:14210 | (ii) cannot in the opinion of the court of appeal conveniently be inquired into before the court of appeal,
-- src:14211 | be referred for inquiry and report, in the manner provided by rules of court, to a special commissioner appointed by the court of appeal;
-- src:14212 | (f) act on the report of a commissioner who is appointed under paragraph (e) in so far as the court of appeal thinks fit to do so; and
-- src:14213 | (g) amend the indictment, unless it is of the opinion that the accused has been misled or prejudiced in his defence or appeal.
@ref s 683(1) (src:14201-14213)
GIVEN power IS A `s 683(1) power`
      `the court of appeal considers it in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the witness would have been a compellable witness at the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the examination was taken under subparagraph (b)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the witness is a competent but not compellable witness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question involves prolonged examination of writings or accounts, or scientific or local investigation, and cannot in the opinion of the court of appeal conveniently be inquired into before it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a commissioner has been appointed under paragraph (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court of appeal is of the opinion that the accused has been misled or prejudiced in his defence or appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 683(1) the court of appeal may exercise the power for the purposes of an appeal under Part XXI` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court of appeal considers it in the interests of justice`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where it considers it in the interests of justice"
    ELSE CONSIDER power
        WHEN `s 683(1)(a) order the production of any writing, exhibit or other thing connected with the proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 683(1)(b) order any witness who would have been a compellable witness at the trial to attend and be examined` THEN
            IF `the witness would have been a compellable witness at the trial` THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any witness who would have been a compellable witness at the trial"
        WHEN `s 683(1)(c) admit, as evidence, an examination that is taken under subparagraph (b)(ii)` THEN
            IF `the examination was taken under subparagraph (b)(ii)` THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an examination that is taken under subparagraph (b)(ii)"
        WHEN `s 683(1)(d) receive the evidence, if tendered, of any witness, including the appellant, who is a competent but not compellable witness` THEN
            IF `the witness is a competent but not compellable witness` THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any witness, including the appellant, who is a competent but not compellable witness"
        WHEN `s 683(1)(e) order that a question be referred for inquiry and report to a special commissioner` THEN
            IF `the question involves prolonged examination of writings or accounts, or scientific or local investigation, and cannot in the opinion of the court of appeal conveniently be inquired into before it` THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "involves prolonged examination of writings or accounts, or scientific or local investigation"
        WHEN `s 683(1)(f) act on the report of a commissioner who is appointed under paragraph (e)` THEN
            IF `a commissioner has been appointed under paragraph (e)` THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the report of a commissioner who is appointed under paragraph (e)"
        WHEN `s 683(1)(g) amend the indictment` THEN
            IF `the court of appeal is of the opinion that the accused has been misled or prejudiced in his defence or appeal` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is of the opinion that the accused has been misled or prejudiced in his defence or appeal"
            ELSE JUST TRUE

