§ `Part XXI -- Powers of the Court of Appeal (sections 686 to 690)`

§§ `Section 686 -- Powers`

-- Every paragraph of 686(1) is a power "on the hearing of an appeal against a conviction or against a verdict that the appellant is unfit to stand trial or not criminally responsible":
-- outside such an appeal the scope limit has no "only", so NOTHING (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05); a failed "where it is of the opinion that" is a where-gate (JUST FALSE, listed).
-- @tag grant=where
-- src:14253 | 686 (1) On the hearing of an appeal against a conviction or against a verdict that the appellant is unfit to stand trial or not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, the court of appeal
-- src:14254 | (a) may allow the appeal where it is of the opinion that
-- src:14255 | (i) the verdict should be set aside on the ground that it is unreasonable or cannot be supported by the evidence,
-- src:14256 | (ii) the judgment of the trial court should be set aside on the ground of a wrong decision on a question of law, or
