-- 686(5): the court before which the new trial is held; paragraph (d) governs "notwithstanding paragraph (a)". Nunavut is (5.01), so NOTHING here ("Subject to subsection (5.01)").
-- The section 553 answer is ccc21's (PLAN.md section 6 seam), taken as a MAYBE BOOLEAN input: a NOTHING there is not turned into FALSE here.
-- @tag fork=F686a
-- src:14281 | (5) Subject to subsection (5.01), if an appeal is taken in respect of proceedings under Part XIX and the court of appeal orders a new trial under this Part, the following provisions apply:
-- src:14282 | (a) if the accused, in his notice of appeal or notice of application for leave to appeal, requested that the new trial, if ordered, should be held before a court composed of a judge and jury, the new trial shall be held accordingly;
-- src:14283 | (b) if the accused, in his notice of appeal or notice of application for leave to appeal, did not request that the new trial, if ordered, should be held before a court composed of a judge and jury, the new trial shall, without further election by the accused, be held before a judge or provincial court judge, as the case may be, acting under Part XIX, other than a judge or provincial court judge who tried the accused in the first instance, unless the court of appeal directs that the new trial be held before the judge or provincial court judge who tried the accused in the first instance;
-- src:14284 | (c) if the court of appeal orders that the new trial shall be held before a court composed of a judge and jury, the new trial shall be commenced by an indictment in writing setting forth the offence in respect of which the new trial was ordered; and
-- src:14285 | (d) notwithstanding paragraph (a), if the conviction against which the accused appealed was for an offence mentioned in section 553 and was made by a provincial court judge, the new trial shall be held before a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX, other than the provincial court judge who tried the accused in the first instance, unless the court of appeal directs that the new trial be held before the provincial court judge who tried the accused in the first instance.
@ref s 686(5) (src:14281-14285)
GIVEN `the court of appeal is the Court of Appeal of Nunavut` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal was taken in respect of proceedings under Part XIX and the court of appeal orders a new trial under Part XXI` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused, in the notice of appeal or notice of application for leave to appeal, requested that the new trial, if ordered, should be held before a court composed of a judge and jury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conviction was made by a provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 553 the offence is within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court of appeal directs that the new trial be held before the judge or provincial court judge who tried the accused in the first instance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 686 court for the new trial`
`s 686(5) the court before which the new trial shall be held` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the court of appeal is the Court of Appeal of Nunavut`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to subsection (5.01)"
        IF NOT `an appeal was taken in respect of proceedings under Part XIX and the court of appeal orders a new trial under Part XXI`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if an appeal is taken in respect of proceedings under Part XIX and the court of appeal orders a new trial under this Part"
        IF `the conviction was made by a provincial court judge` AND `s 553 the offence is within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an offence mentioned in section 553"
        IF `the conviction was made by a provincial court judge` AND `s 553 the offence is within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN (IF `the court of appeal directs that the new trial be held before the judge or provincial court judge who tried the accused in the first instance`
              THEN JUST `s 686(5)(d) the provincial court judge who tried the accused in the first instance`
              ELSE JUST `s 686(5)(d) a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX, other than the one who tried the accused in the first instance`)
        IF `the accused, in the notice of appeal or notice of application for leave to appeal, requested that the new trial, if ordered, should be held before a court composed of a judge and jury`
        THEN JUST `s 686(5)(a) a court composed of a judge and jury`
        IF `the court of appeal directs that the new trial be held before the judge or provincial court judge who tried the accused in the first instance`
        THEN JUST `s 686(5)(b) the judge or provincial court judge who tried the accused in the first instance`
        OTHERWISE JUST `s 686(5)(b) a judge or provincial court judge acting under Part XIX, other than the one who tried the accused in the first instance`

-- 686(5.01): the same for the Court of Appeal of Nunavut: the judge sits "without a preliminary inquiry", and paragraph (d) reads "an indictable offence mentioned in section 553" and "a judge".
-- @tag fork=F686a
-- src:14287 | (5.01) If an appeal is taken in respect of proceedings under Part XIX and the Court of Appeal of Nunavut orders a new trial under Part XXI, the following provisions apply:
-- src:14288 | (a) if the accused, in the notice of appeal or notice of application for leave to appeal, requested that the new trial, if ordered, should be held before a court composed of a judge and jury, the new trial shall be held accordingly;
-- src:14289 | (b) if the accused, in the notice of appeal or notice of application for leave to appeal, did not request that the new trial, if ordered, should be held before a court composed of a judge and jury, the new trial shall, without further election by the accused, and without a preliminary inquiry, be held before a judge, acting under Part XIX, other than a judge who tried the accused in the first instance, unless the Court of Appeal of Nunavut directs that the new trial be held before the judge who tried the accused in the first instance;
-- src:14290 | (c) if the Court of Appeal of Nunavut orders that the new trial shall be held before a court composed of a judge and jury, the new trial shall be commenced by an indictment in writing setting forth the offence in respect of which the new trial was ordered; and
-- src:14291 | (d) despite paragraph (a), if the conviction against which the accused appealed was for an indictable offence mentioned in section 553, the new trial shall be held before a judge acting under Part XIX, other than the judge who tried the accused in the first instance, unless the Court of Appeal of Nunavut directs that the new trial be held before the judge who tried the accused in the first instance.
@ref s 686(5.01) (src:14287-14291)
GIVEN `the court of appeal is the Court of Appeal of Nunavut` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal was taken in respect of proceedings under Part XIX and the Court of Appeal of Nunavut orders a new trial under Part XXI` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused, in the notice of appeal or notice of application for leave to appeal, requested that the new trial, if ordered, should be held before a court composed of a judge and jury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 553 the offence is within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Court of Appeal of Nunavut directs that the new trial be held before the judge who tried the accused in the first instance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 686 court for the new trial`
`s 686(5.01) the court before which the new trial shall be held in Nunavut` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court of appeal is the Court of Appeal of Nunavut`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Court of Appeal of Nunavut orders a new trial under Part XXI"
        IF NOT `an appeal was taken in respect of proceedings under Part XIX and the Court of Appeal of Nunavut orders a new trial under Part XXI`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an appeal is taken in respect of proceedings under Part XIX"
        IF `s 553 the offence is within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an indictable offence mentioned in section 553"
        IF `s 553 the offence is within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN (IF `the Court of Appeal of Nunavut directs that the new trial be held before the judge who tried the accused in the first instance`
              THEN JUST `s 686(5.01) the judge who tried the accused in the first instance`
              ELSE JUST `s 686(5.01) a judge acting under Part XIX, without a preliminary inquiry, other than the judge who tried the accused in the first instance`)
        IF `the accused, in the notice of appeal or notice of application for leave to appeal, requested that the new trial, if ordered, should be held before a court composed of a judge and jury`
        THEN JUST `s 686(5)(a) a court composed of a judge and jury`
        IF `the Court of Appeal of Nunavut directs that the new trial be held before the judge who tried the accused in the first instance`
        THEN JUST `s 686(5.01) the judge who tried the accused in the first instance`
        OTHERWISE JUST `s 686(5.01) a judge acting under Part XIX, without a preliminary inquiry, other than the judge who tried the accused in the first instance`

