§§ `Section 688 -- Right of appellant to attend`

DECLARE `s 688(2) proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `s 688(2)(a) the hearing of the appeal, where the appeal is on a ground involving a question of law alone`
    `s 688(2)(b) an application for leave to appeal`
    `s 688(2)(c) a proceeding that is preliminary or incidental to an appeal`
    `s 688(2) another proceeding`

-- 688(2) is a flat negative closed by "unless rules of court provide that he is entitled to be present or the court of appeal or a judge thereof gives him leave to be present".
-- JUST TRUE here means the bar applies to this appellant in this proceeding.
-- @tag fork=F688
-- src:14314 | (2) An appellant who is in custody and who is represented by counsel is not entitled to be present
-- src:14315 | (a) at the hearing of the appeal, where the appeal is on a ground involving a question of law alone,
-- src:14316 | (b) on an application for leave to appeal, or
-- src:14317 | (c) on any proceedings that are preliminary or incidental to an appeal,
-- src:14318 | unless rules of court provide that he is entitled to be present or the court of appeal or a judge thereof gives him leave to be present.
@ref s 688(2) (src:14314-14318)
GIVEN `the appellant is in custody and is represented by counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      proceeding IS A `s 688(2) proceeding`
      `rules of court provide that the appellant is entitled to be present` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court of appeal or a judge of it gives the appellant leave to be present` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 688(2) the bar on a represented appellant in custody being present applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the appellant is in custody and is represented by counsel`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appellant who is in custody and who is represented by counsel"
        IF proceeding EQUALS `s 688(2) another proceeding`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "is not entitled to be present"
        IF `rules of court provide that the appellant is entitled to be present` OR `the court of appeal or a judge of it gives the appellant leave to be present`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless rules of court provide that he is entitled to be present or the court of appeal or a judge thereof gives him leave to be present"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 688(1): "entitled, if he desires, to be present at the hearing of the appeal", "Subject to subsection (2)": the (2) answer is a MAYBE BOOLEAN input; only a JUST TRUE there (the bar bites) takes the entitlement away.
-- @tag grant=entitled
-- @tag fork=F688
-- src:14312 | 688 (1) Subject to subsection (2), an appellant who is in custody is entitled, if he desires, to be present at the hearing of the appeal.
@ref s 688(1) (src:14312-14312)
GIVEN `the appellant is in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant desires to be present at the hearing of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 688(2) the bar on a represented appellant in custody being present applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 688(1) an appellant who is in custody is entitled to be present at the hearing of the appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the appellant is in custody`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an appellant who is in custody is entitled"
        IF NOT `the appellant desires to be present at the hearing of the appeal`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if he desires, to be present"
        IF `s 688(2) the bar on a represented appellant in custody being present applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (2)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- the bar of subsection (2) is lifted (JUST FALSE) or not engaged (NOTHING: not represented, or a proceeding it does not name): the entitlement stands

