§§ `Section 689 -- Restitution or forfeiture of property`

GIVEN p IS A `Provision of the Code`, n IS A NUMBER, sub IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 689(1) the order is made under the subsection` MEANS p's `section` EQUALS n AND p's `subsection` EQUALS sub

GIVEN p IS A `Provision of the Code`, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 689(1) the order is made under the section` MEANS p's `section` EQUALS n

-- 689(1): the order of compensation, restitution (738, 739) or forfeiture (164.2(1), 462.37(1) or (2.01)) has its operation suspended (a) until the period for notice expires unless the accused waives an appeal, and (b) until a taken appeal is determined.
-- JUST TRUE means suspended; JUST FALSE means not suspended, after the "until" (the until-bar of ruling (d), 2026-11-05).
-- src:14328 | 689 (1) If the trial court makes an order for compensation or for the restitution of property under section 738 or 739 or an order of forfeiture of property under subsection 164.2(1) or 462.37(1) or (2.01), the operation of the order is suspended
-- src:14329 | (a) until the expiration of the period prescribed by rules of court for the giving of notice of appeal or of notice of application for leave to appeal, unless the accused waives an appeal; and
-- src:14330 | (b) until the appeal or application for leave to appeal has been determined, where an appeal is taken or application for leave to appeal is made.
@ref s 689(1) (src:14328-14330)
GIVEN `the order was made under this provision of the Code` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the period prescribed by rules of court for the giving of notice of appeal or of notice of application for leave to appeal has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused waives an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal is taken or an application for leave to appeal is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal or application for leave to appeal has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 689(1) the operation of the order is suspended` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (   `s 689(1) the order is made under the section` `the order was made under this provision of the Code` 738
                OR `s 689(1) the order is made under the section` `the order was made under this provision of the Code` 739
                OR `s 689(1) the order is made under the subsection` `the order was made under this provision of the Code` 164.2 "(1)"
                OR `s 689(1) the order is made under the subsection` `the order was made under this provision of the Code` 462.37 "(1)"
                OR `s 689(1) the order is made under the subsection` `the order was made under this provision of the Code` 462.37 "(2.01)")
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "an order for compensation or for the restitution of property under section 738 or 739 or an order of forfeiture of property under subsection 164.2(1) or 462.37(1) or (2.01)"
        IF ((NOT `the period prescribed by rules of court for the giving of notice of appeal or of notice of application for leave to appeal has expired`) AND (NOT `the accused waives an appeal`))
           OR (`an appeal is taken or an application for leave to appeal is made` AND (NOT `the appeal or application for leave to appeal has been determined`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the expiration of the period prescribed by rules of court"

